{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>I will not let you go, etc.</b> This is what is meant by ״כִּי שָׂרִיתָ וְגוֹ׳ וַתּוּכָל״ — for he prevailed over him, and the angel was unable to depart without his consent. And his saying <b>כִּי אִם בֵּרַכְתָּנִי</b> means that he should not be harmed by the dislocation of his thigh. Or, it may be because he recognized that he was an angel, he sought to obtain his blessing."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:38.699296605Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}